AB  - Recently, semantic change detection (SCD) has received much attention. It is critical to identify not only the changed information but also the semantic maps for two remote sensing images. Previous methods mainly used convolutional neural networks and transformer to extract features. However, they either ignored the correlation between a large number of similar features or were unable to highlight key semantic features, biasing the extracted semantic information. In order to tackle the limitation, we propose a multi scale localized enhanced self-attention transformer (MSLEFormer) for the SCD task, which consists of two sub-task branches, semantic segmentation and change detection. In the semantic branch, our improved multi scale shunt attention and location-free coding FFN layer are able to achieve multi scale detailed learning of global content while highlighting the local features with key semantic information among them. Furthermore, the prediction is performed by the proposed lightweight fusion segmentation head with low computation cost. So that the high-frequency and low-frequency texture features are fully integrated while the correlation between token features is better preserved. In the change branch, we design a hierarchical difference feature fusion module to fully utilize texture features from coarse to fine by fusing difference features layer by layer, which provides a priori guide to the change location for the final semantic prediction map. We evaluated the proposed method on two datasets, the experimental results indicate that the proposed network model achieves good results and achieves superior performance compared to several state-of-the-art methods.
