AB  - Remote sensing image change detection (CD) can identify the surface changes in a certain area by comparing the images of two different time periods. This method has significant application value in many fields such as urban expansion monitoring. With the application of deep learning in the field of change detection, there are many excellent CNN-based and transformer-based models have been developed. However, there is a lack of multimodal change detection dataset, and the text prompts generated by existing multimodal models are not flexible enough. Additionally, the diverse morphology of change objects in change detection tasks may lead to missed detections or inaccurate delineation of change boundaries by the models. To address these issues, this paper proposes a model called ASC-MDFE, which is based on Adaptive Semantic Calibration (ASC) and Multi-scale Difference Feature Extraction (MDFE). The ASC uses the bitemporal image category information generated by CLIP to calculate the difference, and generates an adaptive context on this basis, and then combines it with the text cue to reflect the change for text encoding. The MDFE fuses context information under different receptive fields through cross-scale feature fusion, and combines feature map subtraction and cosine similarity to calculate change features. Thus, multi-scale change information can be extracted from the bitemporal image data. The proposed ASC-MDFE achieves advanced IoU and F1-Score on well-known change detection datasets SYSU-CD (71.81%, 83.59%), LEVIR-CD (86.06%, 92.51%) and LEVIR-CD+(76.25%, 86.52%).
