AB  - This research uses deep convolutional neural networks to classify different types of Indian soil from high-resolution satellite images. Our study examines four main soil types found across India: alluvial, black, desert, and red. For our experiments, we built an image library containing approximately 800 labeled pictures captured by the LANDSAT-8 satellite. These images were collected at various times from each type of soil. The method we propose uses the convolutional layers from previously trained CNN networks (DenseNet121, Efficient-NetB5, Xception, and ResNet50) to extract important features, combined with a newly created fully connected layer and output layer to achieve accurate soil classification. The results of our experiments show that the EfficientNetB5 model performed better than all other networks trained with our proposed framework, achieving the highest testing accuracy of 98.75% when identifying soil types.
