AB  - With the development of technology,deep learning methods have been widely used in the object detection of remote sensing images. However,some remote sensing objects lack labeling data,which makes the learning of few-shot become one of the key problems in the field of remote sensing. In few-shot learning,the amount of image data and annotation is extremely small. The mainstream research often adopts the universal feature enhancement method,without targeted enhancement according to the morphology feature of objects. To solve the above problems,this paper proposes a morphology sensitive feature mining based few-shot oriented object detection method of remote sensing images(FOFM-Net)to enhance the model learning process. The morphology sensitive feature extractor is used to extract RoI features containing background information. Due to the small number of samples,some positive samples are not labeled,then the feature mining module is used to find missing feature blocks. Experiments on DOTA,an open data set of remote sensing images,prove the effectiveness of the method.
