AB  - High-resolution (30 m) daily soil moisture (SM) dataset is critical for precision agriculture, drought monitoring, and water resource management. However, such dataset remains challenging to obtain due to the limited spatial and temporal resolutions in existing satellite products. To address this issue, this study proposes a novel two-step deep learning framework to produce a high-resolution (30 m) daily seamless SM with reliable accuracy, leveraging strengths from open-access remotely sensed products, terrain, and soil property datasets. The framework is independent from in-situ measurements. First, a convolutional neural network-based super-resolution model (MSRNet) downscales 500 m MODIS spectral bands (8 bands including visible, near-infrared, and thermal infrared) to 30 m resolution using Harmonized Landsat-Sentinel (HLS) data of the corresponding 8 bands. Second, a SM simulation network (SMSNet) learns the relationship between SM and 16 explanatory variables, including the downscaled MODIS bands, terrain features, soil properties, and 1 km SMAP/Sentinel SM at an intermediate resolution of 125 m. Third, the trained SMSNet is applied to 30 m inputs to generate seamless daily high-resolution SM estimations. Validated against in-situ measurements in Naqu (central Tibet Plateau) with significance test (p < 0.01), the 30 m SM achieves significant accuracy improvements over the original SMAP/Sentinel product, with increased correlation (R = 0.70 vs. 0.68) and reduced errors (RMSE = 0.09 m3/m3 vs. 0.12 m3/m3, ubRMSE = 0.07 m3/m3 vs. 0.10 m3/m3). Moreover, the cross-regional validation is conducted at the Maqu (northeast Tibet Plateau) for generalizability and transferability test of the established SMSNet, and achieves reasonable performances. This research provides a feasible solution for large spatial–temporal scale improvement of SM simulation through the combination of MSRNet and SMSNet, enabling field-scale SM applications, as demonstrated in the Tibetan Plateau region, without reliance on ground-based networks.
