AB  - In the field of hyperspectral image (HSI) and Light Detection and Ranging (LiDAR) data fusion classification, Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) excel at extracting local features but struggle to capture long-range dependencies. In contrast, Transformers are effective at modeling long-range interactions yet exhibit limitations local feature extraction and computational efficiency. Additionally, existing methods often overlook the varying abilities of shallow and deep network layers to capture dependencies across various scales, as well as the deep interaction between multimodal features. To address these challenges, this paper proposes a Scale-aware Deep Hierarchical Transformer (SaDHT). The SaDHT first leverages convolutional layers to extensively extract local information from HSI and LiDAR data. It then introduces a lightweight and efficient Scale-aware Module (SaM), which consists of a Multi-group Mixed Convolution (MgMC) module and a Scale-aware Aggregation (SaA) module. The MgMC module captures multi-scale features and expands the receptive field, while the SaA module effectively integrates features from different groups. Furthermore, a novel encoder stacking strategy is designed to simulate the evolving dependency relationships across network layers. Finally, cross-token fusion is employed to enhance feature interaction between modalities, further boosting model performance. Extensive experiments on three public datasets demonstrate the competitive performance of SaDHT. The source code will be available at: https://github.com/junhengzhu/SaDHT.
