AB  - At present, the co-classification of hyperspectral images (HSI) and LiDAR data (LiDAR) has become a popular research direction for remote sensing tasks. However, Some existing methods ignore the nonlinear coupling and correlation between different bands, spatial positions, etc. in HSI data when processing it. Moreover, during the process of multimodal data fusion, some methods often lose the locally effective information among multimodal features. Addressing the above questions, this paper designs a interactive adaptive cross-fusion network(IACF-Net) based on the combination of CNN and transformer. The network first adds weight constraints to the HSI data, and then multi-layer convolutional neural network (CNN) was used to extract features from HSI data with different weights and LiDAR data. Secondly, designed a co-attention module(CAM) to realize the information exchange between HSI data and capture correlations between their features, complete the adaptive decoupling. Finally, the cross-attention fusion module (CAFM) is used to fuse HSI and LiDAR features to realize the information exchange between heterogeneous features, while retaining the local useful information. We conducted experiments on IACF-Net on three benchmark HSI and LiDAR datasets. The experimental results show that the overall accuracy (OA) of IACF-Net is higher than other advanced network models, verifying the effectiveness of IACF-Net in the collaborative classification problem of HSI and LiDAR data. This study confirms that the proposed IACF-Net, with its unique ”weighted-interactive-cross fusion” architecture, can effectively overcome the challenges of strong coupling of HSI data and loss of multimodal fusion information, providing a superior performance solution for collaborative classification of HSI and LiDAR data.
