AB  - The authors regret that due to unintentional technical formatting inconsistencies during proofreading and reference management, some references were not accurately reflected in the final published article. Specifically, several references cited in the main text were inadvertently omitted from the reference list. We sincerely apologize for this oversight. The missing references have now been included to ensure completeness and accuracy. These corrections do not affect the scientific content, interpretation, or conclusions of the article. They are provided solely to ensure that all citations are complete, accurate, and properly presented in the bibliography. The article uses a numbered (IEEE-style) referencing system. Because this system follows sequential numbering, adding the omitted references to the original list would alter citation numbering throughout the manuscript. To maintain consistency with the published version, the original numbering has been retained, and the corrections are presented in this corrigendum. Missing References R.A. Castañeda, S. Avlijas, M.A. Simard, A. Ricciardi, Microplastic pollution in St. Lawrence river sediments, Can. J. Fish. Aquat. Sci. 71 (2014) 1767–1771, https://doi.org/10.1139/cjfas-2014–0281 Y. Huang, Q. Liu, W. Jia, C. Yan, J. Wang, Agricultural plastic mulching as a source of microplastics in the terrestrial environment, Environ. Pollut. 260 (2020) 114096, https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envpol.2020.114096 D. Huang, J. Tao, M. Cheng, R. Deng, S. Chen, L. Yin, R. Li, Microplastics and nanoplastics in the environment: Macroscopic transport and effects on creatures, J. Hazard. Mater. 407 (2021) 124399, https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jhazmat.2020.124399 M.M. Hasan, E.H. Jho, Effect of different types and shapes of microplastics on the growth of lettuce, Chemosphere 339 (2023) 139660, https://doi.org/10.1016/j.chemosphere.2023.139660 J. Gong, P. Xie, Research progress in sources, analytical methods, eco-environmental effects, and cont